  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\mathrm{z}_1, \\mathrm{z}_2$ and $\\mathrm{z}_3, \\mathrm{z}_4$ are 2 pairs of complex conjugate numbers, then $\\arg \\left(\\frac{z_1}{z_4}\\right)+\\arg \\left(\\frac{z_2}{z_3}\\right)$ equals:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n0\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\pi$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Consider $\\arg \\left(\\frac{z_1}{z_4}\\right)+\\arg \\left(\\frac{z_2}{z_3}\\right)$\n$$\n=\\arg \\left(z_1\\right)-\\arg \\left(z_4\\right)+\\arg \\left(z_2\\right)-\\arg \\left(z_3\\right)\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&=\\left(\\arg \\left(z_1\\right)+\\arg \\left(z_2\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\arg \\left(z_3\\right)+\\arg \\left(z_4\\right)\\right) \\\\\n&\\quad \\operatorname{given}\\left(\\begin{array}{l}\nz_2=\\bar{z}_1 \\ \\\\\nz_4=\\bar{z}_3\n\\end{array}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\left(\\arg \\left(z_1\\right)+\\arg \\left(\\bar{z}_1\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\arg \\left(z_3\\right)+\\arg \\left(\\bar{z}_3\\right)\\right) \\\\\n&\\qquad\\left\\{\\begin{array}{l}\n\\operatorname{also}\\left(\\arg \\left(\\bar{z}_1\\right)=-\\arg \\left(z_1\\right)\\right. \\\\\n\\arg \\left(\\bar{z}_3\\right)=-\\arg \\left(z_3\\right)\n\\end{array}\\right\\} \\\\\n&=\\left(\\arg \\left(z_1\\right)-\\arg \\left(z_1\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\arg \\left(z_3\\right)-\\arg \\left(z_3\\right)\\right) \\\\\n&=0-0=0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
}